README for the WebOS port of ScummVM
------------------------------------

SUPPORTED DEVICES

  Tested on Palm Pre (WebOS 1.4.5). Should work on Palm Pre 2, Palm Pixi,
  and HP TouchPad running WebOS 3.x, though only the Pre has been verified.

INSTALLATION

  Install the .ipk through Preware or the WebOS Quick Install tool.

  When starting ScummVM the first time it creates the following directory
  structure on the USB storage:

    ScummVM/
      Extras/
      Games/
      Plugins/
      Saves/
      Screenshots/
      Themes/

  To install games, switch your device to USB drive mode and copy game
  folders into ScummVM/Games. Then start ScummVM, tap "Add Game", and
  select the folder.

  Plugins (.so files) are installed automatically under
  /media/cryptofs/apps/usr/palm/applications/org.scummvm.scummvm/lib/

CONTROLS

  Default mode: Direct Touch
  -------------------------
  The touchscreen operates in direct-touch mode by default. The cursor
  is invisible; tapping moves the cursor to the exact touch position
  and registers a click there.

    Single tap              Left click at tap position
    Hold 0.5s + release     Left click (auto-drag mode: hold starts drag)
    Two-finger tap          Right click
    Three-finger tap        Middle click

  Two-finger swipe gestures (both fingers moving same direction):

    Swipe left              Escape key
    Swipe right             Toggle trackpad mode on/off
    Swipe up                Show on-screen keyboard (WebOS 2/3 only)
    Swipe down              Open ScummVM main menu

  Three-finger swipe gestures:

    Swipe right             Toggle auto-drag mode on/off
    Swipe down              Spacebar (pause/unpause)

  Trackpad mode (toggle with two-finger swipe right)
  --------------------------------------------------
  The visible cursor moves relative to finger motion, like a laptop
  trackpad. Use this for games that need precise cursor positioning.

    Drag one finger         Move cursor
    Tap (< deadzone drift)  Left click
    Hold 0.5s               Start drag (auto-drag mode)
    Two-finger tap          Right click
    All swipe gestures      Same as direct-touch mode

  Keyboard modifiers:

    Shift, Ctrl             Standard modifier keys on the physical keyboard
    Hold gesture area       Alt (orange key is consumed by WebOS)
    Gesture area back       Escape
    Gesture area forward    (passed through as keycode 229)

AUTO-DRAG MODE

  Auto-drag is on by default. When you hold a tap for more than 0.5
  seconds without moving, ScummVM holds the left mouse button down so
  you can drag objects. Lift your finger to release.

  Toggle auto-drag with a three-finger swipe right. A status message
  confirms the new state.

AUDIO

  This build links against the PDK-provided SDL audio. The following
  audio formats are supported:

    MIDI          Yes (built-in software synthesizer)
    PCM/WAV       Yes
    OGG Vorbis    No  (libtremor not built)
    MP3           No  (libmad not built)
    FLAC          No  (libFLAC not built)

  Games that use OGG or MP3 music will run silently for those tracks.
  Many such games still display subtitles and are fully playable.

BUILDING FROM SOURCE

  Requirements:
    - WebOS PDK installed at /opt/PalmPDK
    - WebOS SDK installed at /opt/PalmSDK/0.2
    - Linaro GCC 4.9.4 ARM cross-compiler
      (prefix arm-linux-gnueabi-, targeting ARMv6 softfp)
    - The host must have ar, ranlib, nm in the Linaro toolchain bin dir

  The Linaro toolchain is required (not a newer GCC) because the WebOS
  device ships glibc 2.5 and only supports symbols up to GLIBC_2.4.
  GCC 5+ generates GLIBC_2.17+ symbols (clock_gettime, etc.) that will
  cause "symbol not found" crashes at launch. GCC 4.9.4 stays within
  GLIBC_2.4 for all code paths ScummVM uses.

  Configure (run from a separate build directory):

    export WEBOS_PDK=/opt/PalmPDK
    export WEBOS_SDK=/opt/PalmSDK/0.2
    export PATH=<linaro-bin>:$PATH
    /path/to/scummvm/configure \
      --host=webos \
      --enable-plugins \
      --default-dynamic \
      --enable-release

  Then edit config.mk to replace short tool names (arm-linux-gnueabi-g++
  etc.) with full Linaro paths if they are not first in PATH.

  Build and package:

    make -j$(nproc)
    make package

  The .ipk is created in portdist/.

KNOWN ISSUES AND TECHNICAL NOTES

  Phantom touch events
  --------------------
  Aging webOS hardware (particularly Palm Pre units) generates spurious
  SDL_MOUSEBUTTONDOWN / SDL_MOUSEMOTION / SDL_MOUSEBUTTONUP event cycles
  for touch slot 0 with no finger on the screen. This manifests as:

    - In trackpad mode: the cursor drifts left then slowly upward
    - In direct-touch mode: button presses appear to do nothing

  The fix (in backends/events/webossdl/webossdl-events.cpp):
    1. If a BUTTONDOWN arrives for finger 0 while a click is already
       pending (_fingerDown[0] true and _doClick true), it is phantom
       and is discarded without moving the cursor.
    2. Motion events in direct-touch mode during a pending click are
       discarded (return false) so they cannot relocate the cursor.
    3. The cumulative-drift click-cancellation deadzone is only applied
       in trackpad mode; in direct-touch mode the drag timer handles
       intentional drags.

  This was not an issue with original 2.1.0 hardware (less wear), but
  is required for devices used since 2019.

  Screen layout
  -------------
  The Palm Pre screen is 320x480 (portrait). ScummVM defaults to 2x
  scaling, producing a 640x400 virtual overlay displayed letterboxed
  in a 320x200 physical area centered on the screen. The top and
  bottom ~140 pixels of the physical screen are unused dead zones.

  glibc compatibility
  -------------------
  See "BUILDING FROM SOURCE" above. Never use system GCC (5+) to build
  for this target; always use the Linaro 4.9.4 cross-compiler.
